  {
   "type": "text",
   "id": 11,
   "title": "Command Reference",
   "gridPos": {
    "h": 20,
    "w": 24,
    "x": 0,
    "y": 40
   },
   "options": {
    "mode": "markdown",
    "content": "### Writing a command\n\nThe command runs with `/bin/sh -c` in the alerter container, as user **nobody**, for each alert -- at most `ALERTING_PARALLEL` (4) at a time, killed after `ALERTING_COMMAND_TIMEOUT` (20 s) together with anything it started. `curl`, `wget` and `jq` are installed; `/tmp` is the only writable place. Quote the variables (`\"$ALERT_TITLE\"`): titles carry whatever an attacker put in a hostname or an SSID.\n\n| Variable | Contents |\n|---|---|\n| `ALERT_SOURCE` | `suricata`, `dns`, `arp`, `wids`, `scan`, `reputation` |\n| `ALERT_TYPE` | what happened: `suricata.alert`, `dns.blocked`, `arp.gateway_spoof`, `wids.evil_twin`, `scan.internal`, `reputation.outbound`, ... (`<source>.test` for Send test) |\n| `ALERT_SEVERITY` / `ALERT_SEVERITY_NAME` | `1`..`4` / `critical`, `high`, `medium`, `info` |\n| `ALERT_TITLE` | one line, ready for a chat message |\n| `ALERT_DETAILS` | `key: value` lines -- every detail below |\n| `ALERT_JSON` | all of it as one JSON object: post it as it is |\n| `ALERT_TIME`, `ALERT_EPOCH` | when it happened (UTC) |\n| `ALERT_SITE`, `ALERT_URL` | `ALERTING_SITE`, and a dashboard link when `ALERTING_GRAFANA_URL` is set |\n| `ALERT_REPEATS` | how many of the same alert the cooldown held back before this one |\n| `ALERT_TEST` | `1` for Send test |\n| `ALERT_SRC_IP`, `ALERT_DST_IP`, `ALERT_SIGNATURE`, `ALERT_SID`, `ALERT_QNAME`, `ALERT_LIST`, `ALERT_IP`, `ALERT_MAC`, `ALERT_BSSID`, `ALERT_SSID`, `ALERT_INTERNAL_IP`, `ALERT_REMOTE_IP`, `ALERT_FEED`, ... | each detail of the alert, upper-cased (whichever the source has) |\n| `ALERT_SECRET_<NAME>` | from `alerting.env` on the host, so a token never has to be typed here, where every viewer can read it |\n\n**Examples**\n\nAny JSON webhook: `curl -fsS -m 10 -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d \"$ALERT_JSON\" \"$ALERT_SECRET_WEBHOOK\"`\n\nSlack / Mattermost / Teams-style text: `jq -n --arg t \"[$ALERT_SEVERITY_NAME] $ALERT_TITLE\" '{text: $t}' | curl -fsS -m 10 -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d @- \"$ALERT_SECRET_SLACK\"`\n\nntfy: `curl -fsS -m 10 -H \"Title: $ALERT_SOURCE_NAME\" -H \"Priority: $((6 - ALERT_SEVERITY))\" -d \"$ALERT_TITLE\" https://ntfy.sh/$ALERT_SECRET_NTFY_TOPIC`\n\nOnly critical ones to a pager, everything to chat: `[ \"$ALERT_SEVERITY\" = 1 ] && curl ... \"$ALERT_SECRET_PAGER\"; curl ... \"$ALERT_SECRET_CHAT\"`\n\nA non-zero exit is recorded as `failed` with the command's output in *Recent Alerts* -- `curl -f` makes an HTTP error count as one.\n"
   }
  }
